    "title": "LESSON 12: POSSESSIVE PRONOUNS",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Possessive pronouns show ownership:",
          "",
          "mein  = my        unser = our",
          "dein  = your      euer  = your (plural)",
          "sein  = his/its   ihr   = their",
          "ihr   = her       Ihr   = your (formal)",
          "",
          "THEY WORK LIKE 'EIN' (take same endings):",
          "          Masc    Fem     Neut    Plural",
          "NOM:      mein    meine   mein    meine",
          "AKK:      meinen  meine   mein    meine",
          "",
          "EXAMPLES:",
          "Das ist mein Hund. (my dog - masc nom)",
          "Ich sehe deinen Hund. (your dog - masc akk)",
          "Das ist meine Katze. (my cat - fem)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lektion zwölf"
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "MORE POSSESSIVE EXAMPLES:",
          "",
          "MASCULINE:",
          "Wo ist dein Bruder? (Where is your brother?)",
          "Ich kenne seinen Vater. (I know his father)",
          "",
          "FEMININE:",
          "Das ist meine Schwester. (This is my sister)",
          "Er liebt seine Mutter. (He loves his mother)",
          "",
          "NEUTER:",
          "Wo ist mein Buch? (Where is my book?)",
          "Sie liest ihr Buch. (She reads her book)",
          "",
          "PLURAL:",
          "Das sind unsere Kinder. (our children)",
          "Ich mag eure Ideen. (I like your ideas)"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "013",
    "trigger_word": "Hand",
    "trigger_card_number": 310,
    "title": "LESSON 13: IMPERATIV (COMMANDS)",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Commands depend on who you're addressing:",
          "",
          "DU-FORM (informal singular):",
          "Drop 'du' and the -st ending:",
          "du kommst → Komm! (Come!)",
          "du wartest → Warte! (Wait!)",
          "a→ä verbs lose the umlaut:",
          "du fährst → Fahr!  du schläfst → Schlaf!",
          "s-stems drop only -t: du liest → Lies!",
          "",
          "IHR-FORM (informal plural):",
          "Use ihr-form, drop 'ihr':",
          "ihr kommt → Kommt! (Come!)",
          "",
          "SIE-FORM (formal, singular & plural):",
          "Use Sie-form, keep 'Sie' after verb:",
          "Kommen Sie! (Come!)",
          "Gehen Sie! (Go!)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lektion dreizehn"
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "SPECIAL CASES:",
          "",
          "SEIN (to be) - irregular:",
          "du → Sei ruhig! (Be quiet!)",
          "ihr → Seid ruhig!",
          "Sie → Seien Sie ruhig!",
          "",
          "HABEN (to have):",
          "du → Hab Geduld! (Have patience!)",
          "ihr → Habt Geduld!",
          "Sie → Haben Sie Geduld!",
          "",
          "SEPARABLE VERBS - prefix goes to end:",
          "auf|stehen → Steh auf! (Get up!)",
          "mit|kommen → Komm mit! (Come along!)",
          "",
          "SOFTEN COMMANDS with 'bitte' or 'mal':",
          "Komm mal her! (Come here - friendly)"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
