    "trigger_card_number": 319,
    "title": "LESSON 14: PLURAL FORMATION",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "German nouns form plurals in FIVE main ways:",
          "",
          "1. Add -e:  der Tisch → die Tische",
          "2. Add -en/-n:  die Frau → die Frauen",
          "3. Add -er:  das Kind → die Kinder",
          "4. Add -s:  das Auto → die Autos",
          "5. No ending (sometimes + umlaut):",
          "   der Lehrer → die Lehrer",
          "   der Apfel → die Äpfel",
          "",
          "ALL plurals use \"die\" (regardless of gender)",
          "",
          "HINTS (not rules!):",
          "• Masc./neuter in -er, -el, -en → no ending",
          "• Feminine often → -en (die Frau → die Frauen)",
          "• Neuter: -e or -er (das Jahr → die Jahre)",
          "• Nouns in -e → -n (die Minute → die Minuten)",
          "Always learn a noun WITH its plural."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lektion vierzehn"
      }
    ]
  }
]
